Looks like what happened was:

- You started eating something while full, which set up the "You're finally
  finished" message for when you could move again. (The global variable
  "nomovemsg" is set to the message to use.)
- Something interrupted your eating, so the message was not displayed
  and the variable was not reset.
- You then started to read the book, and failed, which made you unable
  to move.  Failing to read the book does not set the nomovemsg variable,
  so it was still set to "You're finally finished."
- When you could move again, nethack displayed the message in nomovemsg,
  which was the wrong one.

This can be easily reproduced in explore mode.

If you hadn't been interrupted, then the nomovemsg would have been reset
to null and a default message ("You can move again") would have been used
instead, which is why this doesn't happen more often.

It's obviously a bug, I would think that nomovemsg just needs to be set to
null when you fail to read a spellbook.  I don't see it in the bug list, but
that list is getting so long that I could have missed it.


